{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-09T22:09:46.324Z","data":{"text":"Task 5 complete.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Added `src/core/web/web-site.ts`** (73 lines):\n- `WebServerSite`, `WebServerStatus` interfaces\n- `readServerStatus` — calls `readWatchState(projectRoot, home)` on every invocation, returns `path: /p/<project>/`\n- `routeWebSite` — pure path mapper: `/` and `/p/<project>` redirect, `/p/<project>/<rest>` → `/<rest>`, else `notFound`\n- `sendSiteRedirect` — 302 with `Location: /p/<project>/`\n\n**Modified `src/core/web/web-server.ts`** (218 → 239 lines):\n- `WebServerOptions.site?: WebServerSite`\n- `handleRequest` consults `routeWebSite` when a site is present; redirects, 404s, or strips the prefix before the existing routing (so static files, documents, SSE, and the actions guard/token/method rules all work under the prefix)\n- `GET /p/<project>/api/server` serves `readServerStatus(...)` via the shared JSON helper (no-store)\n- handle `url` becomes `http://127.0.0.1:<port>/p/<project>/`; without a site everything is byte-for-byte as before\n\n**Added `tests/web-site.test.ts`** covering all four \"Project paths on a server\" scenarios: the full path table, a write through the prefixed actions path with the token, the status document with live service/watcher records re-read between calls, and the no-site behavior.\n\nBoth the task verify and `pnpm verify` (typechecks, build, full test suite, lint) pass."}}
